  "id": "COMPOUND:34419 - PROTEIN:4928",
  "verbalization": "Notoamide B is implicated in the regulation of T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Notoamide B acts as a target of several compounds, which in turn modulate CD3 expression. Specifically, Notoamide B is linked to Malme-3M, a compound that targets Oppsit-4(15)-Ene-1Beta,11-Diol, which ultimately affects CD3. Similarly, Notoamide B is also connected to A498, another compound that targets Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol,3beta-, which also influences CD3. These findings collectively indicate that Notoamide B may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of CD3 expression. The consistent presence of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Notoamide B interacts with CD3 via a complex network of targets, suggesting a potential role in immune-related processes. The mechanistic link is supported by the presence of multiple intermediate targets, reinforcing the idea that Notoamide B may influence CD3 through a multi-step process.",
